    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0775" n="761" xml:id="pg761"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCulloch, Secretary of the Treasury, to Mr. Seward,
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1866-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi>
                        11, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 10th instant, requesting that the vessel called La
                    Orientale, advertised for Montevideo, be detained at New York for examination.
                    In accordance with such request, the following telegram was forthwith
                    transmitted to the collector at New York:</p>
                <p>Detain vessel called La Orientale, which is at pier No. 33 North River, and
                    advertised for Montevideo, and await instructions from this Department.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to inform me at the earliest practicable moment what further
                    action, if any, is required from this Department in the matter.</p>
                <p>I am yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HUGH McCULLOCH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                            Treasury.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
